 | ~~H1~~ (was F-ADM-03) | — | `/api/platform/audit-log` | ✅ FIXED | Audit-log middleware in `services/api-gateway/src/middleware/audit.ts` now captures every authed POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE on `/api/*`. Records: action (e.g. `verification.verify`, `users.update`, `auth.login`), resource_type, resource_id (UUID-validated), actor (req.user.userId), organizationId, IP (X-Forwarded-For first hop or socket), user-agent, success (HTTP 2xx/3xx), tenantId, duration. `/api/platform/audit-log` handler now UNIONs `audit_logs` + `platform_audit_log` so the existing UI shows both sources. Verified end-to-end in browser: Platform Audit Log page lights up with auth.login (success+401), verification.verify, users.update (actor populated). Two known limitations: (a) `/api/auth/login` has actor_id null because http-proxy-middleware streams response bytes without invoking res.json — the next authed request DOES carry req.user, so the chain remains traceable; (b) anonymous endpoints have actor_id null by definition. Both documented in middleware. Follow-up: have auth-service POST /api/audit on login. |
-| ~~H2~~ (was F-API-01 part 2) | — | `/api/anchors/document/:id` | ✅ FIXED | Now returns 404 with no echoed id when no anchors match. Verified: nonexistent id → `404 {"error":"No anchors found"}`; real id → 200 with full anchors array. The gateway function `makeFetchDocFromAnchorStore`, once cited here as the caller that handles a non-200, was retired in KS-1628. Whether a current caller treats a 404 from this route as no anchor is not measured (KS-1840). |
+| ~~H2~~ (was F-API-01 part 2) | — | `/api/anchors/document/:id` | ✅ FIXED | Now returns 404 with no echoed id when no anchors match. Verified: nonexistent id → `404 {"success":false,"error":{"code":"NOT_FOUND","message":"No anchors found"}}`; real id → 200 with full anchors array. The gateway function `makeFetchDocFromAnchorStore`, once cited here as the caller that handles a non-200, was retired in KS-1628. Whether a current caller treats a 404 from this route as no anchor is not measured (KS-1840). |
 | ~~H3~~ (was F-ADM-01) | — | Admin dashboard + "System Health" page | ✅ FIXED (with follow-up) | (a) **Services Online tile** previously showed 3 because originate's `/api/admin/dashboard` only probed auth + anchoring (+self). Removed servicesOnline from that endpoint entirely; frontend now always pulls from `/system/status` (the gateway's authoritative probe across all configured services). Verified in browser: tile now shows **19** of 22 services healthy. Also fixed: `totalVerifications` was counting ALL audit_logs rows; now filters to `WHERE action LIKE 'verification.%' OR resource_type='verification'`. (b) **Sidebar entry** renamed from "System Health" to "Errors & Compliance" with tooltip "System errors, GDPR data-subject requests, retention policies" — accurately describes the page (it has tabs: System Errors / GDPR DSRs / Retention Policies). Verified in browser. **Follow-up**: a real Service Health page (rendering `/system/status` with per-service tiles, last-check time, response latency) is genuinely useful for operators and is tracked separately. |
